<h1><strong>Stipulations of the Framework Contract </strong></h1>
<details>
<summary>See Stipulations </summary>
<h3 id="primera.-objeto"><a href="#primera.-objeto">FIRST.— OBJECT </a></h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>The purpose of this Framework Contract is to establish the general legal regime of accession and
                participation in the ISBE network and the legal relationship between the Adhering Entity and the Managing Entity,
                framework that is applicable to any entity that holds the status of Participant independently
                of the Level(s) of Participation that it assumes. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The specific rights, operational capabilities, limitations and obligations of each Level of
                Participation are developed and specified in the corresponding Role Annexes that, where applicable,
                signed by the Adherent Entity in its capacity as Participant, which form an integral part of
                this Framework Contract and complement it. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The signing of this Framework Contract alone does not confer on the Adhering Entity the status of
                Participant of the ISBE network. To acquire this condition it will be necessary, in any case, the
                simultaneous subscription of the Framework Contract and, at least, one Role Annex relating to one of the
                Participation Levels available, and from that moment on the Adherent Entity will be subject to both
                to the general regime of this Framework Contract as well as to the specific regime of the Role Annex(es).
                subscribed/s. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The subsequent assumption of new Levels of Participation by the Adhering Entity will require
                the signing of the corresponding additional Role Annexes and prior verification by the Entity
                Manager of compliance with the applicable requirements in each case, in accordance with the Policies
                ISBE. The termination of a specific Role Annex will not affect, unless expressly agreed otherwise or
                that it be the only Role Annex, to the validity of this Framework Contract or to the remaining Levels
                of Participation that the Adhering Entity maintains in force. </p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 id="segunda.-definiciones"><a href="#segunda.-definiciones">SECOND.— DEFINITIONS </a></h3>
<p>For the purposes of this Framework Agreement, the following terms will have the meaning set forth below:
        indicates: </p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>ISBE </strong>”: Acronym for Blockchain Services Infrastructure of Spain, blockchain network
                of a public-permitted nature promoted by public administrations and private entities,
                aligned with European guidelines on interoperability and digital trust. Includes a
                set of networks (base network and Use Case networks, among others) designed to support
                applications with different levels of openness and regulatory requirements. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Managing Entity </strong>”: Entity responsible for operational, technical and
                governance of the ISBE network, authorized to sign this Framework Contract on behalf of
                the network. Exercises the corresponding administrative powers, including the admission of
                participants, supervision of compliance with policies and eventual exclusion of Participants due to
                non-compliance. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>ISBE Policies </strong>”: Set of internal policies that govern various aspects of the
                ISBE network and its ecosystem, approved by the Managing Entity in the exercise of its management functions.
                governance. Some of these policies are of internal application to the Managing Entity and to the
                governing bodies of ISBE, while others are mandatory for the Entities
                Adherents in general or for certain Adherent Entities depending on their Level or Levels of
                Participation. The current version of the ISBE Policies and their scope of application will remain
                updated and available through the ISBE portal or other channels enabled for this purpose, without
                prejudice to the specific indication of applicable policies that appears in the tables included in
                each Role Annex. The approval, modification and prevalence regime of the ISBE Policies against
                to this Framework Contract will be the one provided for in clause Seven. The ISBE Policies that, according to
                said information in force at any time, are applicable to the Adhering Entity will be considered
                incorporated into this Framework Contract by reference and will be mandatory for this in
                the scope of their participation in ISBE. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
<strong>“Participant” </strong>: Legal entity that has signed this Framework Contract and, of
                simultaneously or successively, one or more Role Annexes relating to Participation Levels
                planned, having passed the verification process <em>Know Your Business </em>(KYB) and others
                requirements established in the ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Essential </strong>”: Level of Participation that confers on the Adhering Entity a set of
                limited and non-intrusive operational capabilities over the ISBE network, allowing you, under the terms
                that are specified in the ISBE Policies: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>access the private area and
                ISBE portal; <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>use libraries and assistants ( <em>wizards </em>) of
                pre-configured smart contracts in non-programmatic and supervised deployment modes; and <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>use the basic services that ISBE makes available to its
                Participants (including, in their
                case, notarization services and registration of evidence); <strong><em>(iv) </em></strong>use,
                where applicable, the mechanisms for controlled gas procurement that ISBE makes available to this Level
                Participation (faucet or other equivalents); and <strong><em>(v) </em></strong>receive
                administrative communications and functional support through the ISBE private area and the communication channels
                HelpDesk enabled, without authorizing it to operate its own nodes or to interact directly with
                the <em>blockchain </em>beyond the flows enabled and supervised by ISBE. The Entity
                Adherent may assume this Level of Participation when there is <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>subscribed
                the <strong>Annex I – Specific Conditions of the Basic Level </strong>and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>satisfactorily passed the internal admission procedure
                general provided in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>and so on
                Applicable ISBE policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Observer </strong>”: Level of Participation aimed at Adhering Entities with functions
                of supervision, control, audit, investigation or institutional interest, which allows auditing and
                monitor the ISBE network without the capacity to intervene operationally in it or issue transactions.
                This access includes scanning in read-only mode of the state of the ISBE network.
                (blocks, transactions, metrics and aggregate states), as well as the use of analysis tools
                advanced observability made available by the Managing Entity (monitoring panels,
                dashboards and operational records), which allow the Observer to analyze the behavior of the
                system, its stability and the temporal evolution of its main indicators, without powers of
                issuance of transactions or modification of the state of the network and in the terms and with the scope
                established in the ISBE Policies. The Adherent Entity may assume this Level of Participation
                when there is <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>subscribed on <strong>Annex II — Specific Conditions of the Observer Level </strong>and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>satisfactorily passed the internal evaluation procedure and
                eligibility applicable to this Level of Participation, in accordance with the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>the others
                ISBE policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Developer </strong>”: Level of Participation that enables the Adhering Entity to
                design, develop, deploy and maintain Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>about the networks
                ISBE, after passing the approval and technical and regulatory compliance processes
                established in the ISBE Policies. At this Level of Participation, the Adhering Entity may,
                in addition to the functional capabilities associated with the Basic Level as far as they are compatible: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>deploy <em>Smart Contracts </em>own that have passed the tests
                approval provided for in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>;
                <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>use infrastructure services <em>Blockchain-as-a-Service </em>that ISBE makes available to the Developers or that, in its
                case, they are provided with third-party Execution Node Operators; and <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>request the inclusion of your solutions in the service catalog
                and ISBE applications, under the terms and limits defined in the ISBE Policies. The
                Developer will not be authorized to operate its own Execution Nodes or expose infrastructure
                of node under its control in the ISBE network, unless the Adhering Entity has additionally assumed the
                Execution Node Operator Participation Level. The Adhering Entity may assume this Level
                of Participation when there is: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>subscribed on <strong>Annex III – Specific Conditions of the Developer Level </strong>and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>satisfactorily passed the internal approval procedure
                technical and compliance
                planned for this Level in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and other ISBE Policies
                that are applicable. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Execution Node Operator </strong>”: Level of Participation that enables the Entity
                Adherent to deploy, configure and operate one or more Execution Nodes of the ISBE network
                (other than Consensus Nodes), assuming an infrastructure role within the ecosystem. In
                this Level of Participation, the Adhering Entity may, in the terms established in the
                ISBE Policies: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>use your Execution Nodes as an access point
                transactional to the ISBE network for their own
                systems and applications (for example, through RPC endpoints, APIs or specific connectors); <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>provide, when permitted, connectivity services and <em>Blockchain-as-a-Service </em>to authorized third parties, relying on said Execution Nodes; <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>integrate Execution Nodes into your own delivery systems
                monitoring, event logging, observability and incident management; and <strong><em>(iv) </em></strong>participate in high availability, redundancy and
                resilience that are defined for
                the execution layer of the ISBE network, without intervening in the Consensus Protocol. The Adhering Entity
                that holds this Level of Participation must meet the technical, security,
                bastion, availability, capacity and support that are defined for the Execution Nodes in the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>and in the other ISBE Policies,
                including, where applicable, the obligation to maintain certain service levels (SLAs), maintain
                technical records and collaborate in audits or verifications carried out on the
                infrastructure. The Adhering Entity may assume this Level of Participation when there is: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>subscribed on <strong>Annex IV — Specific Conditions of the Execution Node Operator Level </strong>and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>satisfactorily passed the internal approval procedure
                technical and node management applicable to this Level, in accordance with the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>and the other ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Consensus Node Operator </strong>”: Level of Participation that enables the Entity
                Adherent to operate one or more Consensus Nodes and actively participate in the Protocol
                ISBE network consensus, contributing to transaction validation and security and integrity
                of the infrastructure. At this Level of Participation, the Adhering Entity assumes obligations
                reinforced independence, location, security, availability and compliance with parameters
                of the Consensus Protocol defined in the ISBE Policies. The Consensus Node must be found
                deployed in an identified, stable physical location previously communicated to the Entity
                Manager, located in the territory of a Member State of the European Union or the Economic Area
                European or in any of the territories authorized in the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>, and comply at all times with the
                technical, security, availability and independence conditions established in the Policies
                ISBE. The Adhering Entity may assume this Level of Participation when there is: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>subscribed on <strong>Annex V — Specific Conditions of the Consensus Node Operator Level </strong>; and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>satisfactorily passed the internal approval procedure
                technical, security and governance provided for this Level, in accordance with the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>and the other ISBE Policies,
                including restrictions on the accumulation of roles and segregation of functions that, where applicable, are
                plan for this Level of Participation. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Consensus Protocol </strong>”: Set of rules, algorithms and technical parameters that
                determine how transaction blocks are proposed, validated and finalized on the ISBE network,
                through the exclusive intervention of Consensus Nodes operated by entities that hold the Level
                of Consensus Node Operator Participation and that have been previously authorized in accordance with the
                this Framework Contract and the ISBE Policies. It includes, among other elements, the criteria for
                selection and rotation of Consensus Nodes, quorum and voting rules, necessary thresholds
                for the validation of blocks, the conditions of purpose of the transactions and the procedures
                for the management of incidents and failures in consensus. The definition, review, update and, in
                If applicable, replacement of the Consensus Protocol constitutes a power reserved to the Entity.
                Manager, in accordance with the decisions of the ISBE governance bodies and the Policies
                ISBE, and will be carried out exclusively by means of corresponding software modifications,
                network configurations and/or governance smart contracts. No Participant may alter or
                attempt to unilaterally alter the Consensus Protocol, nor promote bifurcations
                (“ <em>forks </em>") or unauthorized modifications thereof. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Execution Node </strong>”: ISBE network node in charge of processing transactions,
                maintain the state of the blockchain and provide reading services and, where appropriate, issuance of
                transactions, without intervening directly in the Consensus Protocol. It can be operated by the
                Managing Entity or by entities that hold the Participation Level of Node Operator
                Execution, in accordance with the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>and
                the other ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Consensus Node </strong>”: Node that is part of the ISBE network Consensus Protocol,
                responsible for proposing and validating transaction blocks. Its operation is subject to strict
                technical, security (bastioned) and availability requirements defined in the <strong>INF1040 Policy – ​​Node Management Policy </strong>.
            </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Use Case </strong>”: Technological solution (application, service or business process) that
                uses the ISBE infrastructure to execute business logic, record operations and/or anchor
                evidence, normally through one or several Smart Contracts deployed in ISBE networks
                different from the base network. Each Use Case must be previously authorized and approved in accordance with the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, and can, upon request
                of the Adhering Entity that holds the Participation Level of Developer or Node Operator of
                Execution, be included in the ISBE service catalog once deployed. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>Smart Contract </strong>” (Smart Contract): Program or set of codes deployed
                on the ISBE network that automatically executes predefined conditions. Its deployment in the ISBE network
                requires passing a technical and cybersecurity conformity test carried out by the Managing Entity, and
                must be carried out through authorized factory contracts to guarantee traceability and
                compliance with the approved architecture (the “ <strong>Factory Contracts </strong>"). </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>DORA Use Case </strong>”: That Use Case deployed or to be deployed on the ISBE network
                that: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>It is part of the ICT services used by one or more
                financial entities included in the subjective scope of Regulation (EU) 2022/2554
                (“ <strong>DORA Regulation </strong>") for the provision of its regulated services; or <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>is used by
                the Adhering Entity within the framework of a contract with a financial entity subject to the DORA Regulation
                in which you are contractually required to guarantee certain operational resilience requirements
                digital on the infrastructure used, including ISBE. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>DORA Addendum </strong>”: Complementary contractual document to the Framework Contract that incorporates
                the specific clauses required by the DORA Regulation and/or by the subject financial entities
                to the same, in relation to the ICT Services described in the Addendum itself (and its services annex),
                which may correspond to one or more Use Cases deployed on the ISBE network. In the
                DORA Addendum will identify the DORA Use Cases covered, the role of the Adhering Entity in
                said DORA Use Cases and the scope of the additional commitments assumed by the Managing Entity
                for the sole purpose of facilitating compliance with the DORA Regulation by entities
                affected financial institutions and/or the Adherent Entity itself. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
                “<strong>DORA Entity </strong>”: Any entity included in the subjective scope of application of the
                DORA Regulation, whether the Adherent Entity itself or a client of its with respect to which
                deploy a DORA Use Case on the ISBE network. </p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="tercera.-condiciones-generales-de-adhesión-y-participación">
<a href="#tercera.-condiciones-generales-de-adhesión-y-participación">THIRD.— GENERAL CONDITIONS OF
            ADHESION AND PARTICIPATION </a>
</h3>
<p>Las siguientes condiciones generales resultan aplicables a la Entidad Adherente mientras mantenga vigente
        this Framework Contract and has signed at least one Role Annex relating to a Level of
        Participation, regardless of the specific Level or Levels of Participation that, at any given time, it has
        assumed, and without prejudice to what is additionally established in the corresponding Role Annexes. </p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p><strong>Admission and general requirements: </strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>By signing this Framework Contract and, simultaneously, at least one Role Annex
                        relativo a un Nivel de Participación, la Entidad Adherente pasa a integrarse en la red ISBE en
                        the terms provided for in this Framework Contract and in said annex(es). </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adhering Entity declares and guarantees that, at the time of its adhesion and throughout the
                        validity of this Framework Contract, meets the admissibility requirements that, with
                        general or specific for each Level of Participation, establish this Framework Contract and the
                        ISBE policies, including, at least: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>its valid constitution and
                        legal capacity; <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>the exercise of lawful activities; and <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>passing verification processes <em>Know Your Business </em>(KYB) <a class="footnote-ref" href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1 </sup></a>and other verifications that, in a reasonable and proportionate manner, are required in accordance with
                        the applicable regulations and the ISBE Policies in force at all times. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Managing Entity may verify at any time the maintenance of these requirements,
                        may require for this purpose the provision of updated documentation, in accordance with
                        what is established in the ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>ISBE Policy and Regulatory Compliance </strong></p>
<p>The Adhering Entity undertakes to respect at all times the regulations that apply to it,
                the Statutes of the ISBE network (if they exist) and all the ISBE Policies that, according to the information
                published by the Managing Entity on the ISBE portal and the provisions of the Role Annexes that it has.
                subscribed, are applicable to your situation at all times. </p>
<p>In particular, the Adhering Entity will be obliged to comply with: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>the
                ISBE Policies identified by the Managing Entity as generally applicable to all
                Adherent Entity with a current Framework Contract; and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>regarding each level
                of Participation that has been assumed, the ISBE Policies whose scope of application includes said Level
                of Participation. </p>
<p>The regime for approval, modification and updating of the ISBE Policies will be as provided in the
                Seventh clause of this Framework Contract, which the Adhering Entity declares to be aware of and accept. The
                relevant or repeated breach of the ISBE Policies, or of the general obligations derived
                of this Framework Contract, may give rise to the measures provided for in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>,
                including, where appropriate, the suspension of services, the revocation of one or more Levels of
                Participation or forced withdrawal of the Adhering Entity. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Access, credentials and communications </strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>The Managing Entity will provide the Adhering Entity with the access credentials <a class="footnote-ref" href="#fn2" id="fnref2" role="doc-noteref"><sup>2 </sup></a>necessary to access the ISBE portal and the interfaces that are enabled for the management
                        of their participation in the network. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>For the purposes of contractual and operational communications, the channels enabled by the Entity
                        Manager will be, at least, the following: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>the ISBE Private Area,
                        as the main and contractually binding channel of internal communication, through which
                        official notifications, critical operational communications will be distributed
                        (including changes and alerts) and access will be given to the private document center and tools
                        support such as the Help Desk; <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>the official email
                        designated by the Adherent Entity, which will be used as a secondary or reinforcement channel to
                        informative communications, calls or notices that complement the available information
                        in the Private Area; and <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>a periodic newsletter,
                        merely informative, which may be sent by email to registered members
                        of the ecosystem. </p>
<p>Through these channels, the Adherent Entity may manage its relationship with the Entity.
                        Manager and with the ISBE network, including, in particular, the processing of requests for
                        accession, modification or renunciation of Participation Levels by subscribing,
                        modification or resolution of the corresponding Role Annexes, as well as the receipt of
                        notifications and communications related to network operations and Policies
                        ISBE. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adherent Entity will be responsible for the diligent custody of its credentials and the
                        correct management of authorized users under their scope of control, responding to
                        the Managing Entity and against third parties for the use they make of them, unless proven
                        of theft, loss or misuse duly notified to the Managing Entity in the terms
                        that the ISBE Policies provide. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>General financial contributions </strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>As a contribution to the sustainability of the network, the Adherent Entity must pay the fees
                        of membership, fees or charges that ISBE's economic model provides, both on a
                        general as well as, where appropriate, specifically associated with the Participation Levels that have been
                        assumed or the services consumed. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The amounts, concepts, periodicity and payment conditions of said economic contributions
                        will be determined in accordance with the provisions of this Framework Contract, in the Role Annexes and
                        in the ISBE Policies, and will be communicated to the Adhering Entity with reasonable advance notice,
                        applying objective and non-discriminatory criteria in all cases. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adherent Entity undertakes to promptly satisfy all its financial obligations
                        in accordance with the quantities and deadlines notified to you. Failure to pay within the terms
                        provided for in this Framework Contract and in the ISBE Policies may constitute a breach
                        serious contractual and enable the Managing Entity to adopt measures to suspend
                        services, revocation of Participation Levels or forced withdrawal, without prejudice to the
                        claim for amounts owed. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>General liability and proper use of the network </strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>The Adherent Entity is responsible for using the ISBE infrastructure in good faith, with full
                        respect for current legislation, for the rights of other entities participating in the network
                        and to the principles of integrity, security and stability of the infrastructure. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>In particular, the Adhering Entity will refrain from: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>use the
                        ISBE network for illegal activities or activities contrary to public order; <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>introduce malicious code, intentional vulnerabilities or
                        configurations that compromise the security, availability or correct functioning of the
                        network; and <strong><em>(iii) </em></strong>carry out any action that may cause damage
                        the reputation of ISBE or its Participants is relevant. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adherent Entity will hold harmless the Managing Entity and the rest of the entities that
                        participate in the ISBE network against any claim, sanction, damage or cost arising from
                        of his own actions or omissions in the ISBE network or those of the people for whom he must
                        respond, without prejudice to the limitations of liability that, where applicable, are established
                        in this Framework Agreement or in the ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
