<h3 id="cuarta.propiedad-intelectual-e-industrial">
<a href="#cuarta.propiedad-intelectual-e-industrial">FOURTH.—INTELLECTUAL AND INDUSTRIAL PROPERTY </a>
</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>The signing of this Framework Contract does not imply any transfer of property rights.
                intellectual or industrial between the Parties. Each Party will at all times retain ownership of
                its pre-existing intangible assets or those developed outside the ISBE network. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The intellectual and industrial property rights over the applications, <em>Smart Contracts </em>,
                codes, technical documentation and any other developments that the Adherent Entity creates,
                deploy or operate in the ISBE network will belong to the Adherent Entity itself or to third parties that
                correspond, without prejudice to the regime of licenses, authorizations, assignments, limitations of use and
                other conditions established in the <strong>Policy NOR1070 – Intellectual Property Policy </strong>, that the Adhering Entity
                declares to know and accept. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The use by the Adhering Entity of the technological infrastructure, software elements and others
                intangible assets owned by the Managing Entity within the scope of ISBE will be subject to the
                licensing regime provided for in the <strong>Policy NOR1070 – Intellectual Property Policy </strong>and in the other ISBE Policies
                that are applicable, said license automatically extinguishing in the assumptions and terms
                planned there. </p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 id="quinta.-confidencialidad"><a href="#quinta.-confidencialidad">FIFTH.— CONFIDENTIALITY </a></h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>The confidentiality regime applicable to the information to which the Parties have access on the occasion
            of the signing and validity of this Framework Contract and/or any of the Participation Levels that
            the Adherent Entity assumes through the corresponding Role Annexes will be governed by the provisions of the <strong>Policy <br/>NOR1050 – Confidentiality Policy </strong>, which the Adhering Entity declares to know and accept and
            which is considered incorporated herein
            Framework Contract by referral. </li>
</ol>
<h3 id="sexta.-protección-de-datos-personales">
<a href="#sexta.-protección-de-datos-personales">SIXTH.— PROTECTION OF PERSONAL DATA </a>
</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>The Parties guarantee full compliance with current regulations on data protection
                personal, in particular Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and the Spanish development legislation (Law
                Organic 3/2018, Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights, and others
                applicable provisions). </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Without prejudice to the foregoing, the detailed regime applicable to the processing of personal data in the
                context of the ISBE network—including, among other things, the assignment of responsible and
                person in charge of processing, information obligations, technical and organizational measures of
                security, management of incidents and security breaches, use of personal data in records <em>on-chain </em>and the conditions for the eventual formalization of commissioning agreements
                treatment—will be governed by the provisions of the Policy <strong>NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>, that the Adhering Entity
                declares to know and accept and that it is considered incorporated into this Framework Contract by reference,
                The Parties are obliged to comply with it at all times to the extent that it is applicable to them. </p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 id="séptima.-duración-modificación-y-terminación-del-contrato-marco">
<a href="#séptima.-duración-modificación-y-terminación-del-contrato-marco">SEVENTH.— DURATION, MODIFICATION AND
            TERMINATION OF THE FRAMEWORK CONTRACT </a>
</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p><strong>Duration and extensions </strong></p>
<p>This Framework Contract comes into force on the date of its signature by both Parties and will have a
                initial duration of <strong>one (1) year </strong>from said date, remaining in force
                as long as the Adhering Entity has signed at least one Role Annex relating to a Level of
                Participation in the ISBE network. </p>
<p>After said initial period, the Framework Contract will be tacitly extended for periods
                successive periods of one (1) year, unless either Party communicates in writing to the other its
                willingness not to extend it, with a minimum notice of three (3) months regarding the date of
                expiration of the initial period or any of its extensions. </p>
<p>Each Role Annex that is signed will form an integral part of the Framework Contract and its validity will be
                subject to this, unless the corresponding Role Annex is terminated
                individually according to their own clauses <a class="footnote-ref" href="#fn3" id="fnref3" role="doc-noteref"><sup>3 </sup></a>. The extinction of the last Role Annex that the Adhering Entity
                remains in force will determine, in
                In any case, the automatic resolution of this Framework Contract on the same date on which that
                produce effects. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Modification of ISBE Policies and prevalence over the Framework Contract </strong></p>
<p>The Adhering Entity recognizes and accepts that the ISBE Policies that develop this Contract
                Marco, as well as any others that appear at any time as current and applicable according to the
                information published by the Managing Entity, will be approved and may be modified, replaced or
                unilaterally repealed by the Managing Entity, in the exercise of its governance functions
                on the ISBE network and in accordance with the rules for adopting agreements of its governing bodies.
                administration and government in force at all times. </p>
<p>The Managing Entity will notify the Adhering Entity of the modifications to the ISBE Policies (for
                through the ISBE portal or other planned channel), indicating the date of entry into force and
                granting, where appropriate, a reasonable period for its implementation when necessary. </p>
<p>The modifications to the ISBE Policies will be fully applicable and binding for the Entity.
                Adherent from the date indicated in the corresponding notification and will be considered development
                technical, organizational and/or regulatory of this Framework Contract, this being understood to be adapted in so far as
                strictly necessary to align with the current version of said ISBE Policies, without this
                means leaving the validity or compliance of the Framework Contract at the discretion of the Managing Entity in
                the terms of article 1256 of the Civil Code. In case of discrepancy or conflict between the
                provided for in this Framework Contract and the content of the current ISBE Policies that result
                applicable to the Adhering Entity, the provisions of said ISBE Policies will prevail to the extent
                that regulate technical, organizational or operational aspects of participation in ISBE, understanding
                the Framework Agreement automatically adapted as strictly necessary to reflect said
                prevalence. </p>
<p>If any update to the ISBE Policies implies a substantial and objective alteration
                burdensome of the contractual obligations of the Adherent Entity, it may express in writing
                your disagreement and, if the discrepancy persists, request voluntary withdrawal before the date of
                entry into force of the corresponding modification, in which case the Contract will be considered terminated.
                Framework without any penalty for the Adhering Entity and without obligation to assume a different amount
                of the amounts accrued until the effective date of resolution. </p>
<p>Outside of what is provided for in the previous paragraphs, any other modification of the clauses of this
                Framework Contract or Role Annexes must be made in writing and by common agreement between the
                Parts. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Termination of the Framework Contract </strong></p>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>
<em><u>Voluntary withdrawal of the Adhering Entity </u></em>
</p>
<p>The Adherent Entity may, at any time, terminate its participation in the network.
                        ISBE and, therefore, terminate this Framework Contract, notifying the Managing Entity in writing.
                        with a minimum notice of fifteen (15) calendar days, in accordance with the procedure for
                        voluntary withdrawal provided for in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
                    </p>
<p>The technical and operational aspects of the disconnection process and <em>offboarding </em>(including, where applicable, revocation of access, disabling of nodes and
                        delisting of services or Use Cases) will be governed entirely by the provisions of the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
<em><u>Resolution for non-compliance and forced withdrawal </u></em>
</p>
<p>The Managing Entity may agree to the termination of this Framework Contract and the forced withdrawal of
                        the Adherent Entity of the ISBE network in the assumptions and conditions provided for in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>,
                        when there is a serious or repeated breach of the obligations derived from the
                        Framework Contract, the Role Annexes or the ISBE Policies that are applicable. </p>
<p>The procedure, phases, deadlines, hearing guarantees and decision regime applicable to the
                        forced withdrawal will be those established in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>. The
                        forced dismissal due to non-compliance does not exclude the possible claim for damages if the
                        action of the Adhering Entity would have caused certain damage to the Managing Entity, to the network
                        ISBE or third parties. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>
<em><u>Effects of termination of the Framework Contract </u></em>
</p>
<p>The termination of this Framework Agreement, for any reason, will not affect those
                        stipulations that by their nature must subsist, including, but not limited to, the
                        related to confidentiality, protection of personal data, intellectual property,
                        limitations of liability and conflict resolution regime, as well as any
                        others that are provided for in this Framework Contract or in the ISBE Policies. </p>
<p>The Adherent Entity recognizes that, after leaving the ISBE network, it will not have the right to claim
                        compensation or indemnity for the loss of the status of Participant or for the
                        discontinuation of their Use Cases on the network, without prejudice to the eventual return of
                        economic guarantees that, if applicable, had been established and had not been applied to the
                        coverage of defaults or outstanding debts under the terms established in the Policies
                        ISBE. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
