<h3 id="octava.-régimen-específico-para-casos-de-uso-dora">
<a href="#octava.-régimen-específico-para-casos-de-uso-dora">EIGHTH.— SPECIFIC REGIME FOR USE CASES
            DORA </a>
</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>When the Adhering Entity intends to deploy or exploit one or more Use Cases on the ISBE network
                DORA, must, prior to the production deployment of said DORA Use Cases, subscribe
                with the Managing Entity the corresponding DORA Addendum. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The DORA Addendum will have a complementary nature with respect to this Framework Contract and the
                ISBE policies. In case of contradiction between the provisions of this Framework Contract or the Policies
                ISBE and the provisions of a DORA Addendum, the latter will prevail exclusively in relation to the
                DORA Use Cases expressly identified therein, applying the Framework Contract and Policies
                ISBE generally in everything else. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adhering Entity undertakes not to deploy or exploit any DORA Use Case in production.
                on the ISBE network while it is not in force, between the Managing Entity and the Adhering Entity,
                a DORA Addendum that expressly covers said DORA Use Case. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The Adhering Entity will notify the Managing Entity without delay of the concurrence or possible
                concurrence of the circumstances that determine the qualification of a Use Case as a Use Case
                DORA, in accordance with the definitions of this Framework Contract and the DORA Addendum, committing to
                suspend or not start the production exploitation of said DORA Use Case until the Addendum
                corresponding DORA is subscribed. </p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 id="novena.-ley-aplicable-y-resolución-de-conflictos">
<a href="#novena.-ley-aplicable-y-resolución-de-conflictos">NINTH.— APPLICABLE LAW AND RESOLUTION OF
            CONFLICTS </a>
</h3>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p>This Framework Contract, the Role Annexes that comprise it and the ISBE Policies that develop it
                They will be governed and interpreted in accordance with Spanish common legislation. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>For the resolution of any conflict, discrepancy or claim arising from the interpretation or
                execution of this Framework Contract, its Role Annexes or, as applicable, the Policies
                ISBE, the Parties will try, in advance, to reach a friendly solution through the
                ISBE governance channels. </p>
<p>To this end, either Party may notify the other of its position in writing, initiating
                a period of <strong>direct negotiation </strong>thirty (30) calendar days from receipt
                of said notification. During this period, at least one meeting will be held - in person or
                telematics—convened by the Managing Entity, and the Parties must make reasonable efforts to
                reach an agreement. </p>
<p>The friendly solution may optionally be supported by managed voluntary mediation mechanisms.
                by the Managing Entity or by an independent third party. </p>
<p>If, after said period, an agreement has not been reached to end the conflict, each
                intervener, with express waiver of the jurisdiction that may correspond to him, submits to the jurisdiction
                of the Courts and Tribunals of Madrid (or that locality where the Managing Entity has its headquarters).
                registered office, if different), who will be competent to hear the matter. </p>
<p>If by legal imperative the Adhering Entity holds the status of Public Administration and does not
                could be submitted to ordinary civil jurisdiction, the parties agree that any dispute will be
                will be resolved in accordance with the provisions of the public sector contract legislation or
                contentious-administrative, as appropriate. </p>
</li>
</ol>
